# CLI

The binary is `okmate`. The command table in the
[README](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/blob/main/README.md#cli) is the
canonical list.

## Everyday commands

```sh
okmate check knowledge --profile strict --format json
okmate inspect catalog knowledge
okmate inspect concept architecture/system-overview knowledge
okmate inspect graph knowledge
okmate search "system overview" knowledge --profile strict
okmate build knowledge -o dist/knowledge
okmate view knowledge --no-window
okmate roots --format json --no-sync
okmate sync
```

`--format json` is the machine-readable form for `check`, `roots`, and
`timings`. `inspect` and `search` already emit JSON.

Place `--profile` before the `catalog`, `concept`, or `graph` target.

## One root at a time

Pass the bundle directory (or a path the CLI resolves to a root). Do not
expect a single invocation to search every configured root. See
[Multiple bundles](/docs/multiple-bundles/).

## Preview ports

`view` serves localhost. With a window, `--port` defaults to `auto`.
`--no-window` defaults to `8000`. `--public` binds every interface. Settings
POST is loopback-only.
